# Only what lands at the REPO ROOT. Every pattern is anchored with a leading
# slash on purpose: a bare pattern matches at every depth, which is what made
# this file a catch-all governing directories that can speak for themselves.
# ctbrowser/ (and its test/, unittests/, benchmarks/ and examples/),
# third-party/ and tools/ carry their own rules.
/.claude/
Keep `/build*/` at the root and add a `build*/` rule to `ctbrowser/.gitignore` (unanchored is wrong there given the file's stated anchoring rule, so: `/build*/`), e.g. after line 8:

# The CONFIGURE root moved here with the monorepo, so `cmake -B build` typed in
# this directory now makes the build tree HERE. The presets all point at
# ${sourceParentDir}, which the repository root's /build*/ covers.
/build*/

and the same three lines in a new ctcompile/.gitignore.
/examples-*/

# A tool run by hand from the repository root - `tools/check/compare.py`,
# `ctdrive` - drops its screenshot, profile or log HERE. ctest no longer does:
# it runs every test with WORKING_DIRECTORY = ctbrowser/ (CTTest.cmake), which
# ctbrowser/.gitignore covers.
/*.ppm
/*.log
/*.csv
